+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  MAILER Priviledged Commands:                                      |
|                                                                    |
|  CP <cp-command>  - Issue a CP command.                            |
|                                                                    |
|  CMS <cms-command> - Issue any CMS SUBSET command.                 |
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|  FORWARD - Deliver mail to a userid other than the one specified   |
|            in the headers.  It is legal to forward mail to more    |
|            than 1 address.  If you want to continue to receive     |
|            a copy of the mail at your userid, add a forward with   |
|            an address of '<*>'.                                    |
|                                                                    |
|            The 'FOR' option allows an authorized user (anyone in   |
|            the maintainers list) to issue the command 'for' some   |
|            other userid.                                           |
|                                                                    |
|      FORWARD < FOR userid> ADD    destaddr                         |
|                            DELETE destaddr | ALL                   |
|                            LIST                                    |
|                                                                    |
|  QUIESCE - Disable reader file processing.                         |
|                                                                    |
|  ACTIVATE - Reactivate reader file processing.                     |
|                                                                    |
|  RELOAD - Reload routing table and user exits.                     |
|                                                                    |
|  STOP - Stop Mailer (exit program).                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
